# Task 11 - Docker Group Authorization

## Before Group Assignment

### Command

```bash
docker ps
```

### Output

```text
permission denied while trying to connect to the docker API
```

## Cause

User `micah` was not a member of the Docker group.

---

## Fix

### Command

```bash
usermod -aG docker micah
```

### Verification

```bash
su - micah
docker ps
```

### Output

```text
CONTAINER ID IMAGE COMMAND CREATED STATUS PORTS NAMES
```

## Learning

### Authentication

```text
Who are you?
```

### Authorization

```text
What can you do?
```

---

# Task 12 - Create Application Directory

## Command

```bash
mkdir /opt/webapp
```

## Output

```text
File exists
```

## Learning

Directory had already been created.

---

# Task 13 - Change Ownership

## Command

```bash
chown -R micah /opt/webapp
```

## Learning

`chown` changes ownership.

It does not modify permissions.

---

# Task 14 - Change Owner and Group

## Command

```bash
chown micah:docker /opt/webapp
```

## Result

```text
Owner = micah
Group = docker
```

## Learning

```text
user:group
```

format is used with `chown`.

---

# Task 15 - Verify Ownership

## Command

```bash
ls -ld /opt/webapp
```

## Output

```text
drwxrwx--- 2 micah docker ...
```

## Meaning

```text
Owner = micah
Group = docker
Permissions = 770
```

---

# Task 16 - Change Permissions

## Command

```bash
chmod 770 /opt/webapp
```

## Permission Breakdown

```text
Owner  -> rwx
Group  -> rwx
Others -> ---
```

## Learning

`chmod` changes permissions.

`chown` changes ownership.

